[
    {
        "content": "<p>Here are a couple of Nodup and Pairwise theorems I needed, are they worth pushing somewhere? More generally, I have a couple of theorems about a number of core functions on lists (and also <code>List.diff</code> and <code>List.inter</code>), do you personally have a guideline of when you consider it worthwhile to push to mathlib or core when you just stumble on something that might be useful to others without explicitly trying to contribute?</p>\n<p>Otherwise, does anyone have style comments?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unattach_Nodup</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Nodup</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unattach</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Nodup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pairwise</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">zipIdx_Nodup</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zipIdx</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Nodup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pairwise</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of_map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Prod</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">snd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">range_eq_range'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">pairwise_lt_range</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy_Pairwise_aux</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Pairwise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">!</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">loop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Pairwise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">!</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">fun_induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">loop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pairwise_reverse</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy_Pairwise</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Pairwise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">!</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy_Pairwise_aux</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDups_Pairwise</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eraseDups</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Pairwise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">!</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy_Pairwise</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDups_Nodup</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">BEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LawfulBEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">eraseDups</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Nodup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pairwise</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">imp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDups_Pairwise</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 602183536,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1781189338
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think there's the added confusion here that we have both <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.eraseDups#doc\">docs#List.eraseDups</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.dedup#doc\">docs#List.dedup</a></p>",
        "id": 602218067,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781195623
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The second has more theorems</p>",
        "id": 602218096,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781195630
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(and similarly, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.eraseDupsBy#doc\">docs#List.eraseDupsBy</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.pwFilter#doc\">docs#List.pwFilter</a>)</p>",
        "id": 602218243,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781195656
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hm is it possible to prove <code>List.eraseDups l = List.dedup l</code> when we have <code>LawfulBEq</code>?</p>",
        "id": 602230231,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1781198067
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That sounds like the right question, though another option would be to push for deleting one of them</p>",
        "id": 602230869,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781198191
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(i think you should instead target eraseDupsBy and pwFilter, since your statement follows trivially from that)</p>",
        "id": 602230957,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781198208
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it turns out they aren't equal:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- info: [1, 0] -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dedup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: [0, 1] -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eraseDups</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(they aren't modulo List.reverse either)</p>",
        "id": 602248299,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1781201306
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Could you make a PR to <code>dedup</code> adding this example to the docstring?</p>",
        "id": 602251121,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1781201899
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sure, is there a way to submit a pull request without cloning the entirety of mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 602254465,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1781202499
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We have more generally</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy_eq_reverse_foldl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">reverse</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">foldl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">next</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">any</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">next</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">next</span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"n\">acc</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">fun_induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eraseDupsBy</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">loop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 602259270,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1781203513
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"749978\">nrs</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Some.20Nodup.20and.20Pairwise.20theorems.2C.20does.20anyone.20need.20them.3F/near/602254465\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sure, is there a way to submit a pull request without cloning the entirety of mathlib?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You can press <code>.</code> when on Mathlib's GitHub page to open an online editor, or click the pencil icon on the top right of the file you want to edit.<br>\nBoth of these let you submit a PR, but neither of them will let you interact with Lean, but they should work great for docstring changes.</p>\n<p>(if you want to actually run Lean to test code changes you could try GitHub workspaces, but idk what the experience/pricing is)</p>",
        "id": 602271591,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1781206318
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you! Here it is: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40512\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40512</a></p>",
        "id": 602275967,
        "sender_full_name": "nrs",
        "timestamp": 1781207330
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is a recurring problem here. Fortunately, the Batteries version is gone: <a href=\"#narrow/channel/348111-batteries/topic/Where.20should.20List.2Emem_eraseDup.20and.20List.2Emem_eraseDups.20l.2E.2E.2E/with/565087763\">https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/348111-batteries/topic/Where.20should.20List.2Emem_eraseDup.20and.20List.2Emem_eraseDups.20l.2E.2E.2E/with/565087763</a></p>",
        "id": 602340300,
        "sender_full_name": "François G. Dorais",
        "timestamp": 1781225223
    }
]